source	Thomas Aquinas, Summa Theologica I, tr. Fathers of the English Dominican Province (1920), q.2 a.1, objection 2 (the argument of Anselm)
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 17611, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/17611
class	inference
at	S7	Therefore, since as soon as the word "God" is understood it exists mentally, it also follows that it exists actually
fault	from what is understood by the word to what exists: Aquinas replies that it does not follow that what the word signifies exists actually, unless it is granted that something than which nothing greater can be thought actually exists
reference	Aquinas, Reply to Obj. 2 (the same article)
known	canon
